 37	 *       it has seen: that plausible-looking "fix" would have concealed the §11.1 two-origin defect
 38	 *       rather than surfaced it, and {@code StepResult.offsetMs} now forbids it in the contract.
 39	 *   <li><b>{@code 0} is a position, not a missing value.</b> Every check below is an explicit
 40	 *       {@code != null}. A null-coalescing or truthiness-based projection would drop the
 41	 *       browser-start line — the one entry that anchors the timeline.
 42	 *   <li><b>The API rounds once, at persistence.</b> The wire is fractional by §4.3; {@code
 43	 *       offsetMs} and {@code durationMs} are {@code int64} on the public snapshot. No intermediate
 44	 *       rounding, and no second rounding on read.
 45	 * </ol>
 46	 *
 47	 * <p>This class is correct by contract today and correct <em>in fact</em> when story 10.12 lands
 48	 * the injected run clock. Until then a real runner still emits process-origin readings and these
 49	 * derived instants will be absurd. That is the correct behaviour: the defect is upstream and
 50	 * visible, and compensating for it here would install a second, undocumented calibration in the
 51	 * component ADR-002 §11 just ruled must hold none, and it would outlive its cause by years.
 52	 */
